        "topicId": "cons-3-8",
        "conceptId": "porch-roof-section-a",
        "questionRef": "2015 OL Q1(a) — construction and dimensions",
        "stem": "The front porch has a TILED traditional cut roof pitched at 30° and an internal width of 2.0 m. A 400 mm concrete-block wall has a 200 mm full-fill insulated cavity. Rafters and ceiling joists are 200 mm × 40 mm; insulated plasterboard is fixed UNDER the ceiling joists. At scale 1:5, the half-roof section shows one rafter length from 400 mm below the wallplate, through the wall and eaves, to the ridge. Show THREE courses of tiles at eaves and FOUR typical dimensions. The front door is not required. Part (b) shows one method of securing the wallplate to the external wall.",
        "questionText": "To scale 1:5, draw the specified half-roof section, from 400 mm below the wallplate to the ridge, with one rafter length, three tile courses at eaves and four typical dimensions. The front door is not required. This component covers the published construction-detail and dimension marks; the complete drawing has a separate shared quality allowance.",
        "tariffModel": {
          "kind": "fixed"
        },
        "totalMarks": 40,
        "rows": [
          {
            "id": "details",
            "kind": "anyN",
            "verbatim": "Details - typical sizes",
            "marks": 36,
            "contextNote": "Any 9 of the above details (4 marks each). Credit the best NINE acceptable details at 4 marks each, capped at 36. Published examples include ridge board; concrete tiles; battens; overlapped/taped breather membrane; rafters; roof insulation; ceiling joists; insulated plasterboard; wallplate; internal plaster; inner block leaf; full-fill cavity insulation; outer block leaf; external plaster; soffit/fascia; eaves gutter. Preserve the printed 200×40 mm rafters/ceiling joists, 400 mm wall and 200 mm cavity. The source does not divide these 4-mark details into drawing3/annotation1; do not import that Higher-level allocation. The full indicative menu is not mandatory.",
            "group": {
              "claimMax": 9,
              "perOption": 4,
              "options": [
                "Ridge board 250 mm × 35 mm",
                "Concrete tiles",
                "Softwood battens - typical 44 mm × 35 mm",
                "Breather membrane overlapped and taped",
                "Rafters 200 mm × 40 mm",
                "Roof insulation to comply with current Building Regulations",
                "Ceiling joist 200 mm × 40 mm",
                "Insulated plasterboard with skim coat",
                "100 mm × 75 mm wallplate",
                "Internal plaster",
                "Concrete block inner leaf – 100 mm",
                "Full-fill insulated cavity 200 mm",
                "Concrete block outer leaf – 100 mm",
                "Soffit 12 mm and fascia 25 mm",
                "Eaves gutter 100 mm"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "dimensions",
            "kind": "criterion",
            "verbatim": "Four typical dimensions",
            "marks": 4,
            "contextNote": "Include four appropriate dimensions for the specified roof section. This is the published shared 4-mark dimension allowance; no finer partial allocation is printed. Keep the given 30° pitch, 2.0 m internal width and component sizes consistent. The separate whole-drawing quality allowance is not included again here.",
            "permittedMarks": [
